Licensing of this repository
============================

This repository contains four kinds of material under different terms.

1. Code: MIT License (full text below)
   glitchlib/, scripts/, tests/, run_all.py, pytest.ini, config/ (the transcription code and schema).

2. Results: Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International (CC BY 4.0)
   https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/legalcode
   DECISIONS.md, prereg/FROZEN, prereg/data_freeze.json, results/, figures/, logs/.
   Attribution: Deeyan Bothra, "glitch-waiting-time-v2" (see CITATION.cff).

3. Manuscript: copyright reserved
   PAPER.pdf, PAPER_FINAL_REVIEW.pdf and paper/glitch_paper_revised.tex.
   Copyright (c) 2026 Deeyan Bothra. All rights reserved; not covered by the MIT or CC BY 4.0 licences above.

4. Not covered by the licences above (no licence is granted; the terms of the original sources apply)
   - data/raw/glitches.csv: the Jodrell Bank Glitch Catalogue
     (https://www.jb.man.ac.uk/pulsar/glitches/gTable.html; Espinoza et al. 2011, MNRAS 414, 1679;
     Basu et al. 2022, MNRAS 510, 4049). It is included unchanged so that the checksums can be verified.
     data/raw/README.md has been present since the project's files were first committed; its origin is not
     recorded.
   - data/meta/ (README.md, monitoring_gaps.csv, obs_end.csv, pulsar_params.csv, source_audit.csv): input
     tables of the analysis, included so that it can be reproduced. Their initial content (the pulsar rows of
     the CSV tables, the 49 reference rows and n_glitches counts of source_audit.csv, and README.md apart from
     its provenance section) was present when the project's files were first committed on 2026-10-31, and its
     origin is not recorded. The values added since come from the sources cited in the tables: the spin
     parameters from the ATNF Pulsar Catalogue (Manchester et al. 2005, AJ 129, 1993), version 2.9.0; the ends
     of monitoring and the monitoring gap from the published papers named in each row or, where a row names
     none, from the D4g rule; and the source-audit
     entries from an audit table whose compilation is not recorded (see data/meta/README.md). No ownership is
     claimed for this folder.
   - data/processed/ is derived from data/raw/glitches.csv and data/meta/ by the code in this repository. The
     terms of those inputs apply to these tables; CC BY 4.0 covers only what the processing adds.

